SUMMARY:Introduction to Permaculture Design
DESCRIPTION:Introduction to Permaculture Design\nwith Jennifer Verprauskus \nFriday\, October 9  |  10 am – 1pm \nBREG – Core \nRegister Here!\n  \nPermaculture is a design approach that works with nature rather than against it\, creating landscapes that are productive\, resilient\, and regenerative. In this introductory workshop\, participants will learn the foundational ethics and principles of permaculture and discover how thoughtful design can reduce maintenance\, conserve resources\, improve biodiversity\, and create beautiful\, functional outdoor spaces. \nThrough discussion\, examples\, and hands-on exercises\, attendees will explore how to observe natural patterns\, understand site conditions\, and apply simple design strategies to gardens\, homesteads\, and residential landscapes. Whether you are a homeowner\, gardener\, designer\, or simply curious about sustainable living\, this class provides practical tools for creating landscapes that thrive over time. \nJennifer Verprauskus is a North Carolina Licensed Landscape Architect and a Permaculture Design Certificate Holder. She studied Landscape Architecture at the University of Massachusetts & Cal Poly. Since graduating\, she has traveled the world to help people grow trees and their own food. She is the founder of both UpBeet Landscapes and BareRoot Designs\, PLLC. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
